/* book exam traps: High wiper speed comes from the third brush, which leaves fewer conductors and less back emf between the brushes in use; the supply stays 12 V. | The park switch is a cam contact in the gearbox, and it also brakes the motor by shorting the armature; examiners ask for both. | R × C gives seconds only with R in ohms and C in farads: 100 kΩ with 100 µF is 10 s, not 10 ms. | The immobiliser does not usually stop the starter. It withholds the start enable, so the engine cranks but the injectors and coils never fire. | Treating keyless entry and the immobiliser as one system. The fob's rolling code opens the doors; the transponder challenge and response allows the engine to start. */
